 in order to  understand the full extent of oda's 5d  chest moves we have to go all the way  back to chapter one i got into one piece  through the manga and the first time i  saw the gomugomi in chapter 1 of the  story that spiral design on the fruit  itself caught my attention i just felt  like those spirals were put there for a  reason it wasn't just a random artistic  choice there had to be some meaning  behind it however as i read through the  manga i kind of forgot about this and  then as new devil fruits were introduced  a lot of them had some variation of a  spiral design so i just kind of took it  for granted that this is how devil  fruits look  but after the whole nika sun god reveal  and then after the events of the latest  chapters where the gomuko munyami was  thrust into the spotlight i started  looking into ancient symbols that  incorporated a similar spiral design  that is when i found out that extremely  similar spirals to the ones on the  gomugo monomi have been used by multiple  civilizations throughout history to  symbolize the sun in ancient celtic  culture in particular this type of  spiral was likely used to symbolize the  sun and the double spiral which can also  be clearly seen on luffy's devil fruit  was said to represent the sun's journey  over the course of the year with a  specific emphasis on the equinoxes now  just like with the ancient kingdom in  the world of one piece there is a lot we  still don't know about the ancient  civilizations in our own world including  the celts we simply don't know all the  specific meanings that these symbols  held for the ancient people that created  them that said some speculate that  celtic single spirals also symbolized  growth birth and the expansion of  consciousness with the double spiral  also being a symbol for balance and  equality all of these meanings make  perfect sense in the context of luffy  and his devil fruit after quote unquote  dying luffy is born again as joy boy his  devil fruit awakens and his powers and  his consciousness expands after all not  only is luffy now stronger than ever  before but the gorosei implied that in  some sense his powers are only limited  by his own imagination by his own  consciousness there was a bit of  confusion about this part because the  official this translation differs from  the unofficial one but the implication  is that the nika fruit allows  unprecedented freedom of movement and  action for its user so much so that the  fruit's power is considered to be a  godly and in some ways even ridiculous  power furthermore boy's mission dating  back to the void century was to bring  balance and equality to the world  equality to all people and races and  freedom from oppression by the world  government or its predecessors  personally i don't believe that every  single detail in the one piece manga has  some sort of profoundly important  meaning and that literally every panel  is some sort of complex puzzle that oda  intended for us to solve there is such a  thing as looking too deeply into  minuscule details and overthinking  things but with that said luffy's devil  fruit has played an incredibly important  role in the story and that role has only  become more important in the latest  chapters i believe that oda always plans  to have luffy's devil fruit awaken in  this way so i don't think it's too  far-fetched to assume that even in the  first chapter oda drew the devil fruit  with that distinctive spiral pattern for  a reason oda has clearly studied ancient  civilizations and he has implemented  many aspects of these civilizations into  the world of one piece so i'm inclined  to believe that the spiral design on the  gomu gomi aka the nika devil fruit was  an intentional clue about the fruit's  true power but as is often the case with  oda the clue was just vague enough for  us to overlook it until the big reveal  was made and then we finally understood  what oda was doing but only in hindsight  and this doesn't just stop at the design  of luffy's devil fruit in that first  chapter we also saw luffy smiling and  being full of joy after eating the fruit  even though based on everything he knew  about the devil fruit at that point in  time he probably should have been upset  about consuming it rather than being  happy after all luffy's dream was to  become a pirate and sail the high seas  and yet he just found out that he ate a  fruit which not only changed his body  forever but also prevented him from ever  being able to swim not being able to  swim is an absolutely massive handicap  for any sailor and for any pirate not  only that but luffy couldn't really  control his devil fruit powers at first  so it's not like they made him stronger  right away if anything he was taunted  for being weird and a freak due to his  rubber body and he would have to work  hard for years before he learned to  actually control his powers and yet  somehow even as a kid luffy knew that  his newfound powers were a blessing even  though most people in that part of the  world at that point in time would have  considered it a curse luffy felt joy and  he knew that everything would work out  for the best and he was already on his  way to becoming joy boy there were also  many other little hints and clues along  the way that could be considered  foreshadowing for luffy's devil fruit  being related to joy boy nika but a lot  of these were a bit of a stretch no pun  intended nevertheless now that we know  that luffy's devil fruit is not a  paramecia type but rather a mythical  zone type we have to acknowledge that  luffy's attacks and gears were actually  major clues about the true nature of his  devil fruit power initially most of  luffy's attacks were named after weapons  like the gomugamuno pistol and  gomugomuno rocket and this was based on  the fact that back in the first chapter  luffy claimed that his punch was as  powerful as a pistol but then later on  and especially after the time skip we  get more and more techniques named after  animals including a hawk elephant  grizzly python cobra hydra and so on  interestingly enough that most recent  one hydra is a creature from greek  mythology so a mythical animal and then  we have luffy's different forms or gears  these very distinct forms or  transformations were always more in line  with the workings of a zone fruit than  the workings of a paramecia however this  was just overlooked by many because  luffy's devil fruit was assumed to be a  special paramecia like katakuri's  furthermore the fact that luffy's true  power may only be limited by his own  imagination was also hinted at  previously for example in gear third  luffy is able to inflate his bones by  blowing air into his body but your bones  are not actually connected to each other  in a way that would allow air to pass  from one bone to the other and inflate  it so this technique was always more of  a feat of luffy's imagination than  something that made sense in a logical  or scientific way on top of that  throughout the series luffy appears to  be incorporating the techniques of his  rivals into his own powers and abilities  like when he reinterprets the rokushiki  abilities and uses them in his own  attacks this again implies that luffy's  devil fruit ability is not stagnant  rather it is evolving and expanding as  luffy's own experience and imagination  evolve and expand in the past it has  been stated that zone type fruits are  exceptional in terms of their toughness  and recovery speed i believe it was  actually crocodile who said this and if  we look at luffy's abilities it is clear  that his recovery speed and toughness  matches that description but with luffy  being a shonen protagonist i feel like  most of us just assumed that this was  part of his protagonist powers now there  were other clues about luffy's true  power that were more on the nose like  for example the color spread of chapter  1028 which features the straw hats as  gamers slash video game characters on  this page luffy appears to be  representing ken from street fighter but  if you take a closer look at his hair it  is clearly foreshadowing what his hair  will look like in gear 5th so yeah i am  inclined to believe that oda had the  nika fruit in mind since the very  beginning and that he has been teasing  us with it for nearly 25 years that is  definitely a 5d chess move if i ever saw  one but it gets better because we know  that oda has been teasing us and giving  us clues about luffy's true powers since  the beginning it's likely that there are  still more clues out there about the  full extent of his ultimate power that  we are yet to identify in other words  oda may have already told us what full  power luffy will be capable of and how  the story will ultimately end first  let's talk about rubber hose animation  the old animation style that clearly  inspired luffy's new gear 5th abilities  this animation style dates all the way  back to the 1920s and 30s and it is  considered to be the first animation  style that became a standardized style  in america the style is known for  featuring characters whose arms and legs  seem to have the properties of a rubber  hose they can move wildly and they don't  appear to have any bones joints or  wrists essentially this allowed the  characters to move in completely  unrealistic ways and their movements  were not bound by the confines of  science or biology if you heard of  cuphead then you know what rubber hose  animation is because cuphead itself is  an homage to this animation style  although rubber hose animation fell out  of favor as more realistic animation  styles were developed in the 1930s many  of its quote-unquote unrealistic  elements were carried over to future  animations and they are present in such  popular cartoons as the looney tunes  we've all seen those crazy effects when  a cartoon character's eyes pop out of  their head when they're surprised or  scared or the character pulls a giant  thing out of their pockets that couldn't  possibly fit there or the character  pulls up the entire floor from under  them or the character walks calmly on  air and he doesn't fall until the moment  that he realizes that there's nothing  under him road runner tom and jerry bux  bunny daffy duck scooby-doo and many  other classic cartoons are full of this  type of stuff luffy's new powers gear  5th or doneka devil fruit awakening are  clearly based on this type of animation  and actually in chapter 1044 we saw  luffy's eyes pop out we saw him turning  the floor into rubber and pulling it up  from under him to rebound kaido's attack  we saw his limbs temporarily growing to  a ridiculous size and so on this is  certainly an instance of oda paying  tribute to rubber hose animation and it  also adds a brand new flavor to the  story as a whole and to luffy's fighting  style in particular but oda didn't pick  this power just because he liked the art  style there is more to it than that and  this is another thing that has been  hinted at for a very long time in the  story the gorosei state that the power  of the nika fruit is not just possessing  a body with the properties of rubber  although that is a big part of it once  it awakens the nika fruit allows its  user to fight in any way he wants and he  has an incredible amount of strength and  freedom as i mentioned earlier the  user's power is connected to the power  of his own imagination but this devil  fruit had not awakened for over 800  years not since the void century this is  likely because its previous users did  not have the drive and the imagination  to initiate the fruit awakening but  luffy has always had that drive ever  since the very beginning he had big  dreams ever since he was a little kid he  wanted to become the pirate king and the  freest man on the sea and it is this  massive dream that has been guiding him  all this time this dream has given him  the drive to overcome insane obstacles  surpass his limits and do the impossible  in the pursuit of true freedom and that  is why the nika fruit awakened in this  moment  for the first time since joy boy the  nika fruit found a user who has the  vision imagination and determination to  unlock its true power and potential  so in my opinion luffy's new cartoonish  power wasn't just a stylistic choice by  oda gear fifth literally represents true  freedom and not just freedom in the  conventional sense it's not just freedom  to do whatever you want without someone  else stopping you gear fifth symbolizes  freedom from all restraints even the  restraints of reality itself the best  way that i can explain this is by  referring to zen buddhism which has  certainly been a clear inspiration for  oda over the course of the series now i  am not a zen master but i do practice  zazen and this is how i understand it  true freedom means complete  non-attachment it means truly letting go  of everything and this doesn't just mean  letting go of all your material  possessions which is merely the first  step for monks who decide to leave home  and embrace a monastic life letting go  of everything means letting go of all  conceptual thinking all attachment to  quote unquote reality when we say that  something is realistic it means that it  matches up with all of our preconceived  notions about what is possible and  impossible scientific and unscientific  logical and illogical but what if those  preconceived notions did not exist what  if you were like a newborn child  completely free from all classifications  definitions and limitations what if you  looked at the world with a completely  clear and open mind what if the sentence  the birds are flying through the sky and  the sentence the fish are dancing in the  trees were both the same thing to you  and one was not more or less plausible  than the other that would be true  freedom nothing to hold on to nothing to  limit you nothing to classify you or be  classified by you no biases 